# API Requests

A `Request` is the HTTP binding + validation surface, plus a factory to a Domain DTO.

## Each Request file contains

1. A `public const string Permission = "verb_entity";` constant (snake_case, singular entity — `create_company`, `view_tag`, `edit_invoice`) — read by `[HasPermission(RequestClass.Permission)]`. See `authorization.mdc` for the naming conventions.
2. The request properties with default values (never `null!`), bound from body/query/form.
3. A `FromRequest()` method returning the matching Domain DTO (e.g. `CreateXDto`, `UpdateXDto`). If an id comes from the route, use `FromRequest(long id)`.
4. A nested `*RequestValidator : AbstractValidator<TRequest>` in the **same file**, using the extensions in `LoadlyAggregator.API/Validators/Extensions/`.

## Naming

`CreateXRequest`, `UpdateXRequest`, `ListXRequest`, `GetXRequest`, `DeleteXRequest`, `BulkUpdateXStatusRequest`.

## Example (shape mirrors `CreateAdminRequest`)

```csharp
public class CreateAdminRequest
{
    public const string Permission = "create_admin";

    public string FullName { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string UserName { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public List<long>? RoleIds { get; set; }

    public CreateAdminDto FromRequest() => new()
    {
        FullName = FullName,
        UserName = UserName,
        RoleIds = RoleIds
    };
}

public class CreateAdminRequestValidator : AbstractValidator<CreateAdminRequest>
{
    public CreateAdminRequestValidator(IAdminRepository adminRepository)
    {
        RuleFor(x => x.FullName).IsRequiredFullName();
        RuleFor(x => x.UserName)
            .IsRequiredUserName()
            .IsUnique(async u => await adminRepository.GetByUserNameAsync(u) == null,
                      _ => "auth.username_already_taken");
    }
}
```

## Anti-patterns

- ❌ Doing EF/repository work inside `FromRequest()` — it only maps fields.
- ❌ Validating in `FromRequest()` — all validation lives in the FluentValidation class.
- ❌ Duplicating a validation primitive instead of reusing one from `Validators/Extensions/`.
- ❌ Omitting the `Permission` constant on an authenticated endpoint request.
